"external_subprocess_witness","evidence_strength_rank":4,"organ_id":"certificate_kernel_execution_lab","truth_accounting_bucket":"real_runtime_receipt","validator_command":"python -m microcosm_core.organs.certificate_kernel_execution_lab run --input fixtures/first_wave/certificate_kernel_execution_lab/input --out receipts/first_wave/certificate_kernel_execution_lab --acceptance-out receipts/acceptance/first_wave/certificate_kernel_execution_lab_fixture_acceptance.json"},"claim_clause_coverage":{"claim_text_sha256":"493938fca0289f7724ee64e973c33a96849df47b7f689b91fd6463acfd9c4365","clauses":[],"mapped_clause_count":null,"status":"unknown","whole_claim_coverage":"unknown"},"classification":{"evidence_class":"external_subprocess_witness","family":"formal_math_and_proof","real_substrate_disposition":"real_substrate_capsule","truth_accounting_bucket":"real_runtime_receipt"},"component_id":"certificate_kernel_execution_lab","evidence_state":{"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"fresh_replay":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot"},"guide":{"availability":"available","guide_id":"paper_module.certificate_kernel_execution_lab","plain":"Small mathematical claims should be settled by a strict checker, not by taking someone's word. The lab is given small claims about whole numbers, such as 2 + 3 = 5, with some of them deliberately wrong. It builds a small project for Lean, a program that checks mathematical proofs, and has Lean accept or reject each claim, so 2 + 3 = 6 must be refused. The output is a saved record of the build and each result that keeps what Lean accepted apart from other suggestions and leaves out proof text.","plain_availability":"available","ref":"paper_modules/certificate_kernel_execution_lab.md","sha256":"241c92f00943946148fdd50828ae791a90539b3eb513ec9909a3157ea448179e","text":"# Run a small Lean certificate lab\n\n> **In plain terms.** Small mathematical claims should be settled by a strict checker, not by taking someone's word. The lab is given small claims about whole numbers, such as 2 + 3 = 5, with some of them deliberately wrong. It builds a small project for Lean, a program that checks mathematical proofs, and has Lean accept or reject each claim, so 2 + 3 = 6 must be refused. The output is a saved record of the build and each result that keeps what Lean accepted apart from other suggestions and leaves out proof text.\n\nThe certificate lab checks supplied finite certificate examples with a Lean project. Its fixture includes natural-number sum certificates and bounded-order certificates, including deliberately invalid rows. The runner records build and certificate transition results and analyzer metadata in JSON.\n\n## Run the example\n\nFrom the repository root, with Python 3.11 or later and the fixture's Lean and Lake toolchain available:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src python3 -m microcosm_core.organs.certificate_kernel_execution_lab run \\\n  --input fixtures/first_wave/certificate_kernel_execution_lab/input \\\n  --out .microcosm/component-guides/certificate_kernel_execution_lab \\\n  --acceptance-out .microcosm/component-guides/certificate_kernel_execution_lab/acceptance.json\n```\n\nThe fixture route builds the public Lean project in a temporary workspace and checks the declared transitions. The result separates Lean-verified rows from provider suggestions and oracle comparisons. For example, the manifest includes `2 + 3 = 5` and the invalid `2 + 3 = 6`; the latter must be rejected. The tests also check that proof bodies and private source references do not enter the receipts.\n\n## Limits\n\nA successful fixture run supports the stated checks on these certificates, not an arbitrary theorem or a proof of the original research problem. The exported bundle has a separate standalone contract: its test verifies that it does **not** launch Lean or Lake, so a passing bundle result is not a fresh kernel execution. Source-copy digest checks establish matching bytes, not mathematical correctness.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe shown fixture run uses Lean and Lake to check the supplied sum and bounded-order certificate declarations, including `cert_2_3_5_valid`; it does not prove the Python runner correct. `make component-replays` instead uses the standalone exported bundle, with no fresh Lean run, and applies the [Dafny replay admission check](../formal/replay/README.md) to the observed envelope.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Runner](../src/microcosm_core/organs/certificate_kernel_execution_lab.py), [certificate manifest](../fixtures/first_wave/certificate_kernel_execution_lab/input/certificate_manifest.json), [Lean project](../fixtures/first_wave/certificate_kernel_execution_lab/input/lake_project) and [tests](../tests/test_certificate_kernel_execution_lab.py).\n- [Historical fixture result](../receipts/first_wave/certificate_kernel_execution_lab/certificate_kernel_execution_lab_result.json) and [component record](../core/paper_module_capsules.json).\n- [Lean documentation](https://lean-lang.org/documentation/) explains the proof assistant used by the fixture.\n"},"proofs":[],"replay":{"command":"make component-replays","command_ref":"scripts/check/check_component_replays.py","command_scope":"all registered components","configuration_refs":["src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#RUNTIME_STEPS","src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#_accepted_organ_runner_module_refs"],"declared_prerequisites":{"availability_status":"not_assessed_by_index","description":"Lean, Swift and test extras required","source_ref":"Makefile"},"execution_status":"not_run_by_index","fresh_receipt_template":".microcosm/component-replays/<run>/certificate_kernel_execution_lab/exported_certificate_kernel_execution_lab_bundle_validation_result.json","guide_example":{"command":"microcosm certificate-kernel-execution-lab run --input fixtures/first_wave/certificate_kernel_execution_lab/input --out receipts/first_wave/certificate_kernel_execution_lab","expected_result_description":{"status":"unrecorded"},"prerequisites_description":{"see":"paper_modules/certificate_kernel_execution_lab.md","status":"unrecorded"},"scope":"verbatim historical Atlas example; not an execution request and may target retained receipt paths","source_field":"organs[certificate_kernel_execution_lab].first_command","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json","usage":"verbatim_source_example_only","writes_retained_receipts":true},"input_mode":"exported_certificate_kernel_execution_lab_bundle","input_ref":"examples/certificate_kernel_execution_lab/exported_certificate_kernel_execution_lab_bundle","last_result":{"artifact_ref":"receipts/acceptance/first_wave/certificate_kernel_execution_lab_fixture_acceptance.json","artifact_sha256":"7951a6b4500790b534e8e46a37b8a9f4207ba3d2c0ad19739e7a1f26a47a2874","availability":"available","created_at":"2026-06-01T04:18:23+00:00","freshness":"historical_saved_artifact","input_mode":"first_wave_fixture","native_observations":{"execution_witness_mode":null,"lake_available":true,"lean_available":true,"verification_performed":null},"recorded_source_hashes":{},"recorded_status":"pass","source_binding":"not_checked_against_current_replay"},"last_result_selection":"registry current_authority_receipt; not a search for latest ignored run","native_witness_requested":false,"organ_id":"certificate_kernel_execution_lab","prerequisites_ref":"Makefile","prerequisites_status":"not_assessed_by_index","primary_execution":{"argv":["plectis","component-replay","certificate_kernel_execution_lab"],"implementation_state":"companion_external_backend_proposal","input_override_supported":false,"kind":"fixed_component_replay_api","organ_id":"certificate_kernel_execution_lab","output_policy":"fresh ignored .microcosm/component-replays run under selected checkout","scope":"single_registered_component","worker_schema":"plectis_component_replay_worker_v1"},"receipt_name":"exported_certificate_kernel_execution_lab_bundle_v